# Arc Foundry

## Overview

Arc Foundry is an electro-industrial tower-defense game played in the browser on a
derelict substation yard. A runaway surge of conductive scrap, the Load, spills from a
blown feeder vent and crawls toward a grounding collector, and every unit that reaches
the collector costs Grid Integrity. The player defends the yard by stamping salvaged
components out of a scrap-press.

Arc Foundry's defining idea is that a component is never chosen. A stamped rock rolls a
random component type at a random quality the instant it lands, and every rock is also a
wall, so the yard the Load crawls through is the maze the player built out of rolls they
did not pick. Each level yields exactly one firing tower and hardens the rest into inert
blockers, and power comes from folding matched rolls up a five-rung quality ladder and
into recipe-built combination towers.

Arc Foundry has its own name, look, and rules, and its assets, branding, and design are
original to it.

The specification spans several files under `specs/`. `specs/yard.md` gives the tile
grid, the component footprint, and the three maps; `specs/pathing.md` how the Load
crosses the yard and how walls lengthen its route; `specs/enemies.md` the Load roster and
how it scales; `specs/components.md` the eight base component types and the quality
ladder; `specs/combinations.md` the twelve combination towers; `specs/scrap-press.md` the
stamp-and-harvest build loop; `specs/economy.md` Charge and Grid Integrity;
`specs/campaign.md` the wave run and the maze-rating finale; `specs/difficulty.md` the
three difficulties; `specs/hud.md` the status bar and the build panel;
`specs/ui.md` the screens, the menus, and the audio cues; `specs/controls.md` the pointer
and keyboard input; `specs/assets.md` the art, effects, and audio this build produces;
`specs/instrumentation.md` the debug and automation surface; and `specs/showcase.md` the
presentation the finished game ships beside its source. Read all of them and build the
game they describe as one cohesive whole.

