### The build interface

`npm ci` followed by `npm run build` produces the complete static site into `dist/` at the
repository root, with an `index.html` at the root of that directory as the entry point.
The scripts that do this are already in `package.json`.

That directory runs correctly served as-is from any base path, at the root of a static
file server or mounted under a sub-path of one, so every URL the build requests resolves
against the page rather than against the origin root. `specs/assets.md` states the rule
the produced files and the bundled code alike are loaded under.

The build is self-contained. `npm ci` and `npm run build` produce the site from the files
committed in this repository, with the asset-generation tools of `specs/assets.md` absent
from `PATH` and with no network access.

## Goal of this build

Produce a complete, polished, playable game that runs entirely in a browser. Aim for a
game a person would enjoy playing.

The build ships one campaign, played on a map the player chooses from three and at a
difficulty they choose from three. The yard, the Load, the components, the build loop,
the economy, and the debug surface the other spec files describe are the same whichever
map and difficulty are chosen.

